WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.280
All right.

00:04.280 --> 00:09.280
So now it's really important for me that you understand how SQL works with the code with the queries.

00:09.280 --> 00:14.080
So now what I'm going to do I'm going to show you on the right side the syntax of the query in SQL.

00:14.080 --> 00:19.360
And then on the left side I'm going to show you exactly step by step how SQL is going to go and execute

00:19.360 --> 00:19.960
your query.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.680
So now we have the table customers inside our database.

00:22.680 --> 00:26.680
And we will start with the easiest form where we're going to select everything.

00:26.720 --> 00:27.960
Select the star.

00:27.960 --> 00:32.760
So the select star is going to go and retrieve all the columns from your table.

00:32.760 --> 00:37.360
So everything and the From clause is going to tell SQL where to find your data.

00:37.360 --> 00:42.960
So with the select we select the columns that we want and the from you specify the table where your

00:42.960 --> 00:43.960
data come from.

00:43.960 --> 00:45.640
So the syntax can be very simple.

00:45.640 --> 00:48.360
In each query we start always with the select.

00:48.400 --> 00:51.360
And now since we want all the columns we're going to write star.

00:51.400 --> 00:54.160
And with that SQL can understand I want to see everything.

00:54.160 --> 00:56.320
And then after that comes the keyword from.

00:56.320 --> 00:58.920
And now we want to tell SQL where the data come from.

00:58.920 --> 01:01.870
So we have to specify the table name and that's it.

01:01.870 --> 01:03.030
This is all what you need to do.

01:03.030 --> 01:04.950
So once you execute it, what can happen?

01:05.030 --> 01:07.950
SQL can go and execute first the From clause.

01:07.990 --> 01:12.150
So it can go and retrieve all the data from the database to the results.

01:12.190 --> 01:15.590
And then in the next step is going to go and check the select statements.

01:15.590 --> 01:18.150
So which columns we have to keep in the results.

01:18.190 --> 01:21.990
Since you are saying star then the SQL is going to keep everything all the columns.

01:21.990 --> 01:26.310
And with that you will see in the result everything, all the columns and all the rows.

01:26.310 --> 01:27.150
So that's it.

01:27.150 --> 01:28.190
This is how it works.

01:28.230 --> 01:31.670
Now let's go back to SQL in order to select few data from our database.

01:31.710 --> 01:31.950
Okay.

01:31.990 --> 01:33.150
So back to our studio.

01:33.190 --> 01:34.990
Let's go and start a new query.

01:34.990 --> 01:39.430
And let's go and find our database just to expand it and our tables.

01:39.470 --> 01:43.430
Now it is very important to make sure that you are connected to the correct database.

01:43.430 --> 01:47.630
So go to the top left in the menu over here and make sure to select your database.

01:47.630 --> 01:49.030
So my database like this.

01:49.030 --> 01:51.750
Or we have a command for that called use.

01:51.790 --> 01:54.270
And then just write the database name like this.

01:54.270 --> 01:57.430
So I'm telling SQL just use my database like this.

01:57.430 --> 01:59.910
And with that SQL going to switch to your database.

01:59.910 --> 02:04.210
Now if you are learning any new programming language, it is very important to understand about the

02:04.210 --> 02:04.730
comments.

02:04.730 --> 02:09.370
So comments are like notes that you add to your code in order to understand what is going on.

02:09.370 --> 02:12.610
And of course the engine, the database will not go and execute it.

02:12.650 --> 02:15.010
It's going to go and ignore everything inside it.

02:15.010 --> 02:16.930
And there is like two ways on how to do that.

02:16.970 --> 02:21.850
Either you make inline comments by typing two dashes like this and then you write anything.

02:21.850 --> 02:23.570
This is a comments.

02:24.130 --> 02:27.570
So now in SQL if you see it is green that means it is a.

02:27.570 --> 02:28.050
Comments.

02:28.090 --> 02:30.930
Now the other type you can have multiple line comments.

02:30.930 --> 02:36.330
And in order to do that what you can do, you can write slash and then star and then you can write anything.

02:36.330 --> 02:39.850
This and then start a new line is a comment.

02:40.050 --> 02:44.250
So as you can see all the lines after the slash star it is getting green.

02:44.250 --> 02:45.730
That means it is a comments.

02:45.730 --> 02:47.490
And now let's say that you are at the end.

02:47.490 --> 02:50.650
So in order to close it, you write again, star and then slash.

02:50.650 --> 02:53.490
And with that you are telling SQL I'm done with my comments.

02:53.490 --> 02:56.450
So those are the two types of writing comments in SQL.

02:56.530 --> 02:57.610
Now back to our query.

02:57.610 --> 03:01.600
Let's say that we have the following task says retrieve all customer data.

03:01.600 --> 03:06.560
So I would like to see in the results all the data of my customers, everything, all the rows and all

03:06.560 --> 03:07.200
the columns.

03:07.200 --> 03:12.200
So currently our data is stored inside a table called customer, and I need to see all the data in the

03:12.200 --> 03:12.720
output.

03:12.760 --> 03:17.640
In order to do that, we can write a query and all our queries start always with the select.

03:17.640 --> 03:21.680
And since I need everything, all the columns we write star and then a new line.

03:21.680 --> 03:25.640
Let's go and specify for SQL from where it's going to go and get the data.

03:25.640 --> 03:26.840
So it's going to be from.

03:26.840 --> 03:29.440
And then we're going to write the name of the table.

03:29.440 --> 03:32.160
It must be exactly like it is in the database.

03:32.160 --> 03:33.440
So it's called customers.

03:33.440 --> 03:35.520
And you have to have it here as a customers.

03:35.520 --> 03:36.480
So that's it.

03:36.520 --> 03:38.040
Let's go and execute it.

03:38.040 --> 03:43.080
And now if you look to the results you can see we have four columns and five rows.

03:43.080 --> 03:45.520
So with that you are seeing everything inside the table.

03:45.520 --> 03:46.080
Customers.

03:46.080 --> 03:50.440
We can see we have five customers and you can see all the columns about the customers.

03:50.440 --> 03:51.760
So this is very simple.

03:51.760 --> 03:58.160
We have ask question for the database using SQL query and the database that answer our question by returning

03:58.160 --> 03:59.520
our data in the results.

03:59.520 --> 03:59.800
All right.

03:59.840 --> 04:01.310
So now let's move to another task.

04:01.310 --> 04:03.030
I'm going to go and create a new query.

04:03.030 --> 04:05.550
And this time we're going to retrieve all the order data.

04:05.550 --> 04:08.270
So that means I would like to see all the data inside the orders.

04:08.270 --> 04:10.310
So let's go and write a very simple query.

04:10.350 --> 04:12.190
We start as usual with select.

04:12.190 --> 04:17.470
And since we want everything so it is select star from our table orders.

04:17.470 --> 04:18.270
So that's it.

04:18.270 --> 04:19.350
Let's go and execute.

04:19.350 --> 04:22.750
And with that you can see in the output we have again four columns.

04:22.750 --> 04:24.670
But this time we have only four rows.

04:24.670 --> 04:27.150
So that means in this table we have four orders.

04:27.150 --> 04:29.870
And we can see all the data inside this table.

04:29.870 --> 04:34.310
So with that we can understand we have five customers inside our database.

04:34.310 --> 04:37.310
And these customers did generate four orders.

04:37.310 --> 04:39.750
So as you can see we are now talking to our database.

04:39.750 --> 04:42.990
And this is the simplest form of query in SQL.

04:46.950 --> 04:47.270
All right.

04:47.270 --> 04:51.750
So now let's move to the next step in our query where you say you know what I don't want to see all

04:51.750 --> 04:53.150
the columns from the database.

04:53.150 --> 04:54.550
I want to be more specific.

04:54.550 --> 04:58.190
So I would like to select exactly the columns that I need.

04:58.190 --> 05:03.700
So now we want to select few columns from the database, where we select only the columns that we need

05:03.700 --> 05:05.020
instead of everything.

05:05.020 --> 05:07.700
Now about the syntax, we're going to go and change little things.

05:07.700 --> 05:13.620
So instead of using star, we're going to go and make a list of columns that we want to see in the output.

05:13.620 --> 05:15.820
So we're going to select column one column two.

05:15.860 --> 05:17.940
And we're going to separate them using a comma.

05:17.940 --> 05:22.020
So we are just writing a list of columns exactly after the select.

05:22.020 --> 05:23.780
And for the from it's going to stay as it is.

05:23.780 --> 05:24.860
So from a table.

05:24.900 --> 05:26.780
Now if you execute this what's going to happen.

05:26.780 --> 05:28.940
As usual it's going to start with the from.

05:28.940 --> 05:31.300
So it's going to go and get the data from the database.

05:31.300 --> 05:33.940
And then the next step is going to go and check the selects.

05:33.940 --> 05:39.140
So what's going to happen is we're going to go and keep only two columns like for example the name and

05:39.140 --> 05:39.780
the country.

05:39.820 --> 05:44.700
And all the columns that are not mentioned in the select statements will be excluded.

05:44.700 --> 05:50.180
So SQL going to go and remove it from the results and keeps only the columns that we mentioned in our

05:50.180 --> 05:50.660
query.

05:50.660 --> 05:54.380
So this time instead of having four columns in the output we're going to have only two.

05:54.420 --> 05:59.380
So with that you are like filtering the columns and you are selecting exactly what you need.

05:59.380 --> 06:02.330
So now let's go back to your SQL in order to practice this.

06:02.370 --> 06:02.770
All right.

06:02.770 --> 06:04.210
So now we have the following task.

06:04.210 --> 06:08.410
And it says retrieve each customer's name country and score.

06:08.410 --> 06:14.250
So that means I don't want to see everything from the table customers I need only to see the three columns.

06:14.250 --> 06:15.770
So let's see how we can do that.

06:15.810 --> 06:17.490
As usual we start with select.

06:17.490 --> 06:21.930
And I'm going to go with the star in order to see the whole table first from the table customers.

06:21.930 --> 06:24.450
So it's exactly like before let's go and execute it.

06:24.490 --> 06:27.010
And now I can see everything inside the table customers.

06:27.010 --> 06:29.450
But the task says I need only three columns.

06:29.450 --> 06:33.850
So now what we're going to do instead of the star we're going to make a list of columns.

06:33.850 --> 06:37.770
So we start a new line and then we write the name of the first column.

06:37.770 --> 06:42.050
So the first name and a new line for the second column for the country.

06:42.050 --> 06:43.170
And then again comma.

06:43.170 --> 06:44.610
And then we write a score.

06:44.610 --> 06:46.930
So with that we have the three columns.

06:47.090 --> 06:51.410
Now what I usually do I go and select them and give it a push using a tab.

06:51.410 --> 06:53.330
This just looks nicer and easier to read.

06:53.330 --> 06:54.090
So with that we have.

06:54.090 --> 06:56.850
Now between the select and from list of columns.

06:56.890 --> 07:01.950
Now there is like mistake that happens a lot where we go and type a comma after the last column.

07:01.950 --> 07:07.630
So if you do that and execute it, you will get an error because SQL can expect from you a column after

07:07.630 --> 07:08.110
the comma.

07:08.150 --> 07:11.830
And since there is no column and immediately you have a from, you will get an error.

07:11.870 --> 07:14.630
So there is no need for a comma after the last column.

07:14.670 --> 07:16.390
Now let's remove it and execute.

07:16.390 --> 07:19.550
And now that you can see in the output we don't have four columns.

07:19.550 --> 07:20.630
We have only three.

07:20.670 --> 07:22.910
The first name the country and the score.

07:22.910 --> 07:27.550
And by the way they are ordered exactly like you selected in your query.

07:27.550 --> 07:31.910
So first we have the first name and then the country and then the last one the score.

07:31.910 --> 07:34.470
So that means if I go and now change the order.

07:34.870 --> 07:37.950
So let's get the country at the end and execute.

07:37.950 --> 07:40.030
You will see the country at the end.

07:40.070 --> 07:45.990
But I'm going to go and put it back in between to match exactly like the task and remove the last comma.

07:45.990 --> 07:47.150
So execute again.

07:47.150 --> 07:50.190
And with that we have selected few columns from our table.

07:50.190 --> 07:52.510
So we are more specific to what we need okay.

07:52.550 --> 07:55.550
So with that we have covered the two select and from.

07:55.550 --> 08:00.710
Next we are going to talk about the Where clause that you can use in order to filter your data.

08:00.710 --> 08:01.510
So let's go.
